<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Hardened-runtime entitlements for notarized Godot exports.

	Deliberately empty. A GDExtension game usually needs
	com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation because the .app loads a dylib
	the bundle did not sign — but the export pipeline signs the extension with the
	same Developer ID as the bundle, so library validation is satisfied without
	weakening it. Apple has been tightening review on that entitlement; do not add
	it back unless a launch actually fails with a code-signing rejection on the
	extension, and prefer fixing the signature over granting the exemption.

	The app sandbox is off in the export preset, so no network entitlement is
	needed for the WebSocket session. Godot 4 has no JIT, so allow-jit and
	allow-unsigned-executable-memory are not needed either.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
